error[ffi_macro_name]: `sys/select.h` defines `FD_ZERO` as a macro, not a function: a macro has no parameter types for clang to hold this declaration to
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-143-the-fd-set-macros.hero:15:5
     |
  15 |     function FD_ZERO(set: ptr)  #~ ffi_macro_name
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: bind a function of the program's own that calls it: in a header beside this file, `static inline void hero_FD_ZERO(<C type> set) { FD_ZERO(set); }`, with the C types the macro's documentation gives where the placeholders stand; then name that header in an `extern` group and declare `hero_FD_ZERO` there like any function, and clang holds that declaration to your function (§ 13)

